  "title": "Three Lectures on Complexity and Black Holes",
  "authors_raw": "Stanford Institute for Theoretical Physics and Department of Physics",
  "abstract": "This is the written version of three lectures on complexity and black holes given at PiTP 2018 summer program entitled \u201dFrom Qubits to Spacetime.\u201d The \ufb01rst lecture describes the meaning of quantum complexity, the analogy between entropy and complexity, and the second law of complexity. Lecture two reviews the connection between the second law of complexity and the interior of black holes. I discuss how \ufb01rewalls are related to periods of non-increasing complexity which typically only occur after an exponentially long time. The \ufb01nal lecture is about the thermodynamics of complexity, and \u201cuncomplexity\u201d as a resource for doing computational work. I explain the remarkable power of \u201cone clean qubit,\u201d in both computational terms and in space-time terms. The lectures can also be found online at https://static.ias.edu/pitp/2018/ node/1796.html . arXiv:1810.11563v1 [hep-th] 27 Oct 2018",
